(Persona is asking automatically; this is not a user message.) You changed files or ran commands in your last turn but did not say clearly where the work stands, and nobody is following this session now. Do not start new work or continue, and do not push, merge, deploy or message anyone to answer this request. Put such prerequisites in missing. Do only this: describe the work already done and its current state in a block like the one below, then stop.

<closeout status="done|not_done|blocked" merged="yes|no|n/a" deployed="yes|no|n/a">
did: <what changed, one sentence; up to three such lines>
artifact: <pr|commit|branch|doc|build|url|file> <reference>
delivery: <live|pr|merged|off|none; omit when no delivery standard applies>
unblock: <user|agent|other; omit without a delivery gate>
verified: <what you ran or measured and its reading, or "untested">
missing: <what you still need from someone, if anything>
waiting: <for status="blocked": who or what you wait for>
</closeout>

How to fill it in:
- status: done when this turn's work is completed and delivered; not_done when stopped but unfinished; blocked when a person or prerequisite must be awaited, identifying who or what in waiting.
- merged / deployed: facts only. yes only if this exact change was merged or is running in production; otherwise no; n/a when merging or deployment does not apply. These claims will be checked; a false yes is worse than no.
- did: at most three lines, each a plain-language sentence describing a change; omit if nothing changed.
- artifact: one branch, PR, commit, document, build or link per line; omit if none.
- verified: checks or measurements actually run and their readings; write untested if unverified. Never present inference as testing.
- missing: what the user or someone else still needs to supply; omit the line if nothing is missing.
- Copy attribute names, line-leading words and status values exactly; do not translate them. Write content after colons in English.